\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Mechanism classification efficiency. Top plots show results for catalog waveform injections, bottom plots show results for non-catalog injections. Non-catalog injections are considered to be the most realistic test case for a genuine gravitional wave signal from an arbitrary source.}}{12}{}}
\newlabel{fig:eff_mech}{{7}{12}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Classification efficiency for g-mode (left) and SASI (right) waveform features. Performance was better for g-mode classification in our tests, but this is also heavily dependent on the energy of the specific waveform. Overall performance was similar to that of neutrino model mechanism classification.}}{12}{}}
\newlabel{fig:eff_features}{{8}{12}{}{}{}}
